Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Korean particles
Applies after 0057-korean-text.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

Korean build only (GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_KOREAN). The Korean texts follow a
placeholder with a particle placeholder whose form depends on whether the text
before it ends on a final consonant: 은/는, 이/가, 을/를, (으)로, (이)다, 과/와,
아/야 are 0x10-0x16 in field texts and 0x35-0x3B in battle texts. Field
placeholders 0x0E/0x0F are forms of address by the player's gender.
include/hangul.h holds the final-consonant tables of KS X 1001. Korean also puts
"wild" and "foe" before a Pokemon's name, as English does.

